WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:27.949
The Mongolian empire is remembered for their
barbaric conquests, and the power of their

00:00:27.949 --> 00:00:31.619
great leaders that managed to spread the empire
across several continents.

00:00:31.619 --> 00:00:36.370
But one of the most fascinating people who
has been forgotten from the empire is the

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.440
warrior princess Khutulun.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:43.280
She was the great-great granddaughter of Genghis
Khan, and she truly inherited his strength

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:44.470
in battle.

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:49.260
Unlike many other princesses and queens throughout
the history of the world, Khutulun was remembered

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:54.160
for her own glory, rather than the achievements
of a husband or son.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:01.129
She just may have been the strongest Mongolian
warrior of all time.

00:01:01.129 --> 00:01:14.899
The Khan Family Tree
Before we get into the details about the life

00:01:14.899 --> 00:01:19.320
of Khutulun, it's important to go over some
of the details of the Mongolian Empire.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.150
For thousands of years, various tribes in
Mongolia went to war with one another, and

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:26.100
they were never united under one government.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:29.009
Land and horses were taken as spoils of war.

00:01:29.009 --> 00:01:34.120
Women and children were seen as men’s property,
and they were used as trophies of conquest.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:38.610
Powerful men had more than one wife, and chieftains
typically had a harem.

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:42.030
Genghis Khan became the first leader to unite
all of Mongolia.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:46.399
He achieved this by training his army to be
masterful warriors that were stronger than

00:01:46.399 --> 00:01:47.840
any other army in the world.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.680
They trained
falcons to send messages to communicate with

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:54.380
one another, which helped him to spread his
army over vast territories.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:58.860
He pushed his men to train harder to become
a new breed of super-warriors.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:03.700
Genghis Khan once said, “A man's greatest
pleasure is to defeat his enemies, to drive

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:09.110
them before him, to take from them that which
they possessed, to see those whom they cherished

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:15.050
in tears, to ride their horses, and to hold
their wives and daughters in his arms.”

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:19.760
Genghis Khan’s army was so strong, they
were able to defeat the tribes one by one.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:23.950
After uniting Mongolia, he set his sights
much farther than his own country.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.560
He wanted to become the ruler of the entire
world.

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:29.370
He took over parts of Asia, The Middle East,
and Europe.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:33.670
It became the largest empire in the history
of humanity.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:37.300
Even though their army was known for being
ruthless warriors, the Mongolian empire actually

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.739
brought a lot of innovation to the world during
times of peace.

00:02:40.739 --> 00:02:46.650
They were tolerant of all religions, they
encouraged international trade, and diplomacy.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:50.200
Genghis Khan’s had several wives of his
own, and he had many children.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:54.989
His grandson Kublai Khan became the ruler
of Mongolia in the year 1260, and his brothers

00:02:54.989 --> 00:02:58.319
and cousins held positions of power all over
the empire.

00:02:58.319 --> 00:03:03.240
Unfortunately for Kublai Khan, he was not
as feared as his great-grandfather had once

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:07.150
been, and Mongolia would eventually begin
to break off into civil wars.

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:11.670
Kublai Khan would even go to war with his
own brother, Ariq Boke.

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:17.450
A man named Kaidu was Kublai Khan’s cousin,
and the leader of The House of Ögedei.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:21.660
The two cousins disagreed with one another
on how to run the empire, and this would eventually

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.269
cause them to go to war, as well.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:27.980
Kaidu had fourteen sons, but his favorite
child by far was his daughter, Khutulun.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:32.980
And Italian explorer named Marco Polo wrote
down the history of the Mongolian Empire while

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.599
living amongst Kublai Khan’s royal court.

00:03:35.599 --> 00:03:39.700
Most of what is known about Khutlun's life
came from his books, as well as some comments

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:43.019
made by a Persian statesman named Rashid al-Din.

00:03:43.019 --> 00:03:47.489
She was called by several names, including
Aigiarm, which translates to “shining moon.”

00:03:47.489 --> 00:03:51.569
While this is a beautiful name to give to
a baby girl, she would grow up to prove that

00:03:51.569 --> 00:03:58.170
she was far from being a dainty princess.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:05.719
The Wrestling Princess
Because of Genghis Khan’s legacy, future

00:04:05.719 --> 00:04:09.790
generations of Mongolian warriors were trained
to be some of the strongest people on the

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:10.790
planet.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:14.459
If they wanted the Mongolian empire to stretch
across the globe, they needed to be prepared

00:04:14.459 --> 00:04:16.290
to take down any enemy.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:21.139
By the age of 2, boys were already learning
how to shoot bow and arrows and ride on horseback.

00:04:21.139 --> 00:04:23.770
They wrestled one another to learn hand-to-hand
combat.

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:28.680
They practiced both the Chinese martial arts
of Kung Fu as well as ancient Mongolian fighting

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:29.680
techniques.

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:32.220
They weren’t just doing all of this training
on foot, either.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:36.190
All of their fighting techniques also needed
to be executed while riding at high speeds

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:37.200
on horseback.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.930
This included both wrestling and archery.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:43.660
Because of this, their enemies would almost
never be able to knock a Mongolian off of

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:45.919
his horse, no matter how hard they tried.

00:04:45.919 --> 00:04:48.979
In Mongolia, horses are a huge part of their
culture.

00:04:48.979 --> 00:04:52.430
The number of horses actually outnumber the
human population.

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:55.060
People ate horse meat, and drank mare’s
milk.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:58.539
This milk is fermented into an alcoholic beverage
called “airag”, which is considered to

00:04:58.539 --> 00:05:01.590
be the national drink of Mongolia to this
day.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:06.330
There is a saying: “A Mongol without a horse
is like a bird without the wings”.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:10.430
While all of this training, fighting, and
partying was normal for boys, it was almost

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:11.580
never taught to girls.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:16.699
Women were expected to be delicate and subservient
to men while they took care of the farming,

00:05:16.699 --> 00:05:19.240
child-rearing, and household tasks.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:23.550
Khutulun was a tomboy since she was young,
and she wanted to practice fighting with the

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:26.860
boys far more than she was willing to dance
or play with dolls.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:31.590
In his records of his adventures, Marco Polo
describes Khutulun as looking statuesque.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:34.790
She was so tall, one might mistake her for
a giantess.

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:38.129
Since the members of the royal family always
chose the most beautiful women in the country

00:05:38.129 --> 00:05:42.830
to take as their wives, she would have also
been very pretty- most likely looking like

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:44.210
a modern-day supermodel.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:47.789
But unlike most princesses, Khutulun isn’t
remembered for her looks.

00:05:47.789 --> 00:05:50.370
She was known for her incredible wrestling
skills.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:54.110
You could say that she was the world’s first
celebrity female wrestler long before the

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:56.669
age of GLOW and the WWE.

00:05:56.669 --> 00:06:00.699
She was so far ahead of her time, it would
take hundreds of years after her death before

00:06:00.699 --> 00:06:04.650
female wrestling would even be an acceptable
sport around the world.

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:08.509
Mongolian-style wrestling is very different
than what you see on TV, or even what you

00:06:08.509 --> 00:06:09.509
saw in your High School.

00:06:09.509 --> 00:06:11.710
There was no separation of weight class.

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:15.979
Just two people lock arms, and they both try
to push one another over any way they can.

00:06:15.979 --> 00:06:19.919
Imagine arm wrestling, only using your entire
body to push the other person down to the

00:06:19.919 --> 00:06:20.919
ground.

00:06:20.919 --> 00:06:23.819
Once the opponent is knocked to the floor,
the person who remains standing is the winner.

00:06:23.819 --> 00:06:28.020
Because of this, the person’s physical strength
usually determines who the victor will be.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:31.560
Khutulun practiced wrestling and continued
to get stronger every day.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:35.659
She was soon better than any man she had ever
gone up against, and she had the goal of becoming

00:06:35.659 --> 00:06:38.129
the strongest wrestler in the world.

00:06:38.129 --> 00:06:41.919
When she was old enough to get married, several
suitors began to show their interest in making

00:06:41.919 --> 00:06:43.050
her their wife.

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:46.909
Her father, King Kaidu, began to prepare some
eligible suitors for her.

00:06:46.909 --> 00:06:51.230
Khutulun was not afraid to speak her mind
to her father, and rebelliously announced

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:55.370
that she could never marry a man unless he
was able to defeat her in a wrestling match.

00:06:55.370 --> 00:07:00.530
At that time, even princes were not usually
able to choose who their wife would be.

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:05.300
Politics trumped falling in love, and marriages
were usually meant to keep peaceful ties across

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:06.300
the empire.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:10.610
But since she showed so much strength, Kaidu,
gave his daughter his word that she would

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:13.190
be free to marry any man of her choosing.

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:16.860
An official proclamation was written and spread
across the empire, announcing that his daughter

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:20.949
was looking for a husband, as long as he defeats
her in wrestling.

00:07:20.949 --> 00:07:23.370
The entry fee was 100 horses.

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:25.440
If they lost the wrestling match, they would
have to forfeit their horses to The House

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:29.419
of Ögedei, which only increased the wealth
and power of their army.

00:07:29.419 --> 00:07:33.820
Despite the fact that horses are such a huge
part of Mongolian culture, people usually

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:37.030
only had one or two per household, if they
were lucky.

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:39.340
Owning a hundred horses was no simple task.

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:43.120
A man would have had to already come from
some kind of nobility to even collect the

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:44.120
entry fee.

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:48.750
We know that at least one hundred men showed
up at The House of Ögedei to challenge Khutulun

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:52.849
to a match, because she collected a fleet
of over 10,000 horses.

00:07:52.849 --> 00:07:57.099
It’s safe to assume that many of these men
who came to win the match were probably feeling

00:07:57.099 --> 00:07:59.070
overly confident before they arrived.

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:03.039
They probably thought that defeating a princess
would be a piece of cake, but they left feeling

00:08:03.039 --> 00:08:04.080
totally humiliated.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:08.460
It probably took a few matches before the
word spread that this was no ordinary princess,

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:12.689
and that men would need to train before they
could even think about challenging her.

00:08:12.689 --> 00:08:15.971
These wrestling matches were talked about
throughout Mongolia, and many people, like

00:08:15.971 --> 00:08:18.500
Marco Polo, traveled to see the fights.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:21.050
Khutulun would show up wearing a garment called
a cendal.

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:24.870
This was usually worn by men when they practiced
the martial arts, but she would show up wearing

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.990
a version that was made with expensive fabrics.

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:30.130
Her suitors usually showed up wearing a similar
style.

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:33.409
Even though they were fighting, they still
showed up looking their best in front of the

00:08:33.409 --> 00:08:34.409
crowd.

00:08:34.409 --> 00:08:38.820
In the year 1280, when Khutulun was 20 years
old, the son of King Pamar arrived to try

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:41.270
his luck in winning a match against the princess.

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:45.610
The prince offered to wager 1,000 horses instead
of the typical 100.

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:50.210
Marco Polo described him as being young and
incredibly good-looking, and he was surrounded

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:52.050
by an entourage of servants.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:55.440
When he showed up in town and announced that
he wanted to battle Khutulun for her hand

00:08:55.440 --> 00:09:00.120
in marriage, men, women, and children all
showed up to witness this wrestling match,

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:02.170
and it drew the biggest crowd by far.

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:03.930
Her parents were very impressed.

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:09.029
They thought that he was a perfect match for
her, and encouraged Khutulun to lose on purpose,

00:09:09.029 --> 00:09:10.230
so she could marry him.

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:16.181
She replied that she would never lose on purpose
for any fortune in the world.

00:09:16.181 --> 00:09:19.970
The man who was truly worthy of her hand in
marriage would win without her throwing the

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:20.970
match.

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:25.160
To his credit, this prince lasted the longest
out of any other wrestler to ever lock arms

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.490
with Khutulun.

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:30.430
After she slammed the prince onto the palace
floor, the cheering stopped, and the room

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:31.430
went silent.

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:35.450
For the first time ever, the audience was
actually disappointed that she won.

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:39.180
Since he lasted the longest in the wrestling
match out of any other man, maybe Khutulun

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.779
was truly considering if she should throw
the match.

00:09:41.779 --> 00:09:45.750
However, this man was exactly the sort of
husband her father would have arranged for

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:46.750
her.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:49.380
If you think about it, that kind of defeats
the purpose of her being able to choose her

00:09:49.380 --> 00:10:00.200
husband in the first place.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:01.200
Forever Alone?

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.040
After years of kicking ass and taking names,
people began to wonder why Khutulun wanted

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:07.250
to be a single virgin for the rest of her
life so badly.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:08.670
Rumors began to spread about her.

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:13.589
In modern times, one might assume that she
was a lesbian, asexual, or even transgender.

00:10:13.589 --> 00:10:17.320
Despite Mongolia being one of the most progressive
countries in the world at that time, they

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:19.750
were still not accepting of homosexuality.

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:23.710
So it’s very possible that Khutulun had
a strong sense of self, and she wasn’t going

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:27.690
to allow her father to force her into a marriage
that would make her miserable.

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:32.699
At the time, the idea of being a lesbian wasn’t
even an option in the minds of the public.

00:10:32.699 --> 00:10:36.680
Rumors spread that Kaidu may even have had
an incestuous relationship with his daughter.

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:38.740
However, this is probably unlikely.

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.840
Unfortunately, it’s a rumor that was said
of a lot of women back then.

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:45.690
It was just so out of the ordinary that a
daughter was held in such high regard by her

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:48.550
father, and that he allowed her to remain
unmarried.

00:10:48.550 --> 00:10:52.380
The situation was so odd, people simply didn’t
know what to make of it.

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:57.070
According to a Persian statesman named Rashid
al-Din, Khutulun was fighting so hard for

00:10:57.070 --> 00:10:59.820
freedom, because she was in love with a man
named Ghazan.

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:04.260
He was the Mongolian leader of the Persian
territories, and a direct descendent of Genghis

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:05.260
Khan, as well.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:09.310
This meant that they would have been cousins,
and maybe their union would have been forbidden,

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:11.260
because they were too closely related.

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:14.860
Whether the theory was true or not, Khutulun
never did marry Ghazan.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:19.230
He is remembered for converting to Islam,
and setting the new precedent for future rulers

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:20.589
in modern-day Iran.

00:11:20.589 --> 00:11:25.190
He married another princess, named Kokochin,
who was nicknamed The Blue Princess and remembered

00:11:25.190 --> 00:11:26.449
for her stunning beauty.

00:11:26.449 --> 00:11:30.370
Marco Polo helped escort her across the desert
to meet her new husband.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:34.760
Khutulun would have been the polar opposite
of the dainty, frail princess Kokochin.

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:39.029
It’s possible that her heart belonged to
a man she couldn’t have.

00:11:39.029 --> 00:11:43.760
We never do learn if Khutulun got married,
if she remained unmarried having affairs with

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:48.240
men, or if she was secretly enjoying a harem
of her own Most historians believe that she

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:52.139
was single for the rest of her life, because
a royal wedding surely would have been on

00:11:52.139 --> 00:11:53.200
record somewhere.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:57.199
What we do know, though, is that if she got
married, she would never be allowed to live

00:11:57.199 --> 00:12:01.149
out her one true passion in life, which was
to be a warrior.

00:12:01.149 --> 00:12:04.230
And she continued to do just that.

00:12:04.230 --> 00:12:11.829
Going to War
Just like the male Mongolian warriors of her

00:12:11.829 --> 00:12:16.339
day, Khutulun participated in many battles
alongside her father and his army.

00:12:16.339 --> 00:12:20.259
Since she was lighter than a male rider, she
was able to gallop in on her horse at faster

00:12:20.259 --> 00:12:23.920
speeds than her male counterparts, and she
was just as strong.

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:28.209
Marco Polo describes her technique of galloping
up to an enemy soldier on the opposite side

00:12:28.209 --> 00:12:32.820
of the battlefield, picking him up with just
one hand, and lifting his body off the ground

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:36.949
while on horseback and delivering the enemy
back to her side of the battle.

00:12:36.949 --> 00:12:41.880
She was like a hawk flying in on its prey,
and the enemy was understandably terrified

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:42.880
of her.

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:47.180
Kaidu Khan felt that Khutulun was the best
warrior in his army, and she would have been

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:48.880
the most capable leader.

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:53.710
She was even given a silver medallion called
a gergee to wear around her neck, that is

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:56.930
like the modern-day equivalent to becoming
a decorated general.

00:12:56.930 --> 00:12:59.670
She is the only Mongolian woman to ever hold
that honor.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:02.070
Let’s just appreciate that statement for
a moment.

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:06.579
For Kaidu to say that his daughter was the
strongest warrior in the entire army is a

00:13:06.579 --> 00:13:07.579
big deal.

00:13:07.579 --> 00:13:11.269
Even in modern times, it would be almost unheard
of to say that a woman is stronger than any

00:13:11.269 --> 00:13:17.350
entire army full of men, and the Mongolians
were born and bred to be war machines.

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:21.779
Even though Kaidu Khan wanted to appoint Khutulun
as his successor, putting a woman in charge

00:13:21.779 --> 00:13:23.360
was against the rules.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:26.899
This was fine by Khutulun, though, because
she was much more at home on the battlefield

00:13:26.899 --> 00:13:28.910
than in a diplomatic position.

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:32.930
Despite her hesitation to take over the throne
as a young woman, she still attended her father’s

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:37.459
court and was present for all of the important
meetings, so she was well aware of the local

00:13:37.459 --> 00:13:38.459
politics.

00:13:38.459 --> 00:13:42.269
The matter was dropped, and her brothers all
expected that one of them would be declared

00:13:42.269 --> 00:13:45.220
the next Khan whenever their father passed
away.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:50.480
In the year 1301, King Kaidu was dying, and
his dying wish was for Khutulun to take over

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:51.530
as Khan.

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:56.700
Even though he had 14 sons, none of them could
possibly be as good of a military and political

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:58.070
leader as his daughter.

00:13:58.070 --> 00:14:03.199
He attempted to break all Mongolian traditions
and appoint Khutulun as his true heir.

00:14:03.199 --> 00:14:05.790
At this point, Khutulun was 41 years old.

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:10.329
She had years of experience behind her, and
she was respected and feared amongst the army.

00:14:10.329 --> 00:14:15.200
She was old enough now to feel that she was
ready to take on the role as leader, too.

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:17.519
However, her brothers weren’t having it.

00:14:17.519 --> 00:14:22.000
A man named Duwa was given the position as
the new Khan of their territory.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:27.480
In 1306, Khutulun was killed, and there is
no record as to exactly how she died.

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:31.041
Considering that she had a following of soldiers
who respected her, it’s possible that there

00:14:31.041 --> 00:14:34.009
was a power struggle, and that she was killed.

00:14:34.009 --> 00:14:38.740
Most of you may have never heard of Khutulun
until now, and that’s probably because there

00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:42.329
is very little information from people who
actually knew her.

00:14:42.329 --> 00:14:47.410
Marco Polo and Rashid al-Din are the only
two historians who were around in the 1200’s

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:51.959
to write down the details of her life, and
each of them only devoted maybe one or two

00:14:51.959 --> 00:14:54.579
pages of their books to her story.

00:14:54.579 --> 00:14:59.430
Despite the fact that she was barely mentioned
in these texts of the Mongolian empire, the

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:03.850
story of her strength was so fascinating,
it was still passed along by both Mongolian

00:15:03.850 --> 00:15:06.970
and Chinese people by word of mouth.

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:11.520
Just like a childhood game of telephone, her
story was convoluted over the years.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:16.990
In the 1700’s, a French writer named François
Pétis de la Croix wrote stories from Asia

00:15:16.990 --> 00:15:20.579
for a western audience, and he included a
version of Khutulun’s story.

00:15:20.579 --> 00:15:25.480
Only, in his telling, she was a Chinese princess
named Turadot who refuses to marry a man unless

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:27.170
he could solve three riddles.

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:29.069
If they fail, they die.

00:15:29.069 --> 00:15:31.550
This story was eventually made into an Italian
opera.

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:36.079
Khutulun also briefly appeared in the Netflix
series Marco Polo, but it barely scraped the

00:15:36.079 --> 00:15:39.440
surface of how truly awesome she actually
was.

00:15:39.440 --> 00:16:00.379
We hope that the true story of Khutulun, the
warrior princess, will live on.

